exit 0
--- stdout
oikade-host: Run the host: the one process per home that runs your home and its
plugins, and serves Matter and the API.

Everything you run from your laptop, from deploy to status, is oikade.

Usage:
  oikade-host [FLAGS]

Flags:
  --api-addr ADDRESS             Where to serve the API over TLS, for clients
                                 with a token, such as :8443. Empty serves it
                                 only on the socket.
  --broker URL                   The MQTT broker --outside-plugins speak the
                                 contract on. A plugin your home imports, such
                                 as Zigbee2MQTT, takes its broker in its Config.
  --broker-password-secret NAME  The secret with the password for --broker,
                                 whose URL names the user. A password in a flag
                                 lands in ps.
  --data-dir DIR                 Directory with all the host's state. (default
                                 /var/lib/oikade)
  --event-log-age DURATION       How long oikade replay's event log keeps
                                 events. (default 336h)
  --event-log-mib MIB            The most oikade replay's event log holds, in
                                 MiB. (default 64)
  --heartbeat-timeout DURATION   How long your process may go without answering.
                                 (default 10s)
  --home BINARY                  Your home's binary, until one is deployed.
  --matter-interfaces LIST       Comma-separated interfaces to advertise Matter
                                 on. Empty means every multicast interface.
  --matter-port PORT             The Matter bridge's UDP port. 0 turns Matter
                                 off. (default 5540)
  --metrics-addr ADDRESS         Where to serve metrics and health over HTTP.
                                 Empty serves neither. (default :8080)
  --outside-plugins LIST         Comma-separated plugins that run as processes
                                 of their own and speak the MQTT contract on
                                 --broker, under oikade/v1/<name>.
  --plugin-set-timeout DURATION  How long a plugin's Set may run before the
                                 plugin counts as hung. (default 30s)
  --secrets-dir DIR              Directory of secrets, one file each. Defaults
                                 to secrets in --data-dir. A read-only one is
                                 fine.
  --settle DURATION              How long a new version must stay up. (default
                                 5s)
  --simulate FILE                JSON file of simulated devices. Lines of JSON
                                 on stdin change them.
  --stop-timeout DURATION        How long stopping may take before the rest is
                                 cut off. Keep it under systemd's
                                 TimeoutStopSec. (default 10s)

Commands:
  client add  Print a code for oikade login, or a token for CI, from the host
              running here.
  install     Install this binary as the host under systemd, or upgrade the one
              there.
  version     Print this oikade-host's version.

oikade-host COMMAND --help says more of one.

Example:
  oikade-host --data-dir /srv/oikade --api-addr :8443
--- stderr
